Local modification notice

On 2026-08-30, this distribution intentionally modified the vendored SKILL.md
and eferences/cover-prompt-blueprint.md. The local adaptation distinguishes
source facts, user-authored visible copy, and unapproved suggested copy;
requires user approval before derived titles or subtitles become visible;
defaults exact-copy work to a text-free base image plus deterministic
typography when compatible tools are available; validates the actual rendered
pixels for exact, readable, uncropped text; reports generated text as passed,
failed, or not tested separately from image generation; bounds retries; narrows
discovery to cover images and reusable cover prompts. Standalone posters,
flyers, key visuals, and generic poster prompts route directly to
punk-poster-layout when they explicitly need structural composition control.
Article, social, and platform covers remain with punk-cover even with
poster-like treatment; when they explicitly request focal flow, grids,
image-text relationships, or density, punk-poster-layout serves only as a
subordinate structural step. The skill auto-selects exactly one eligible catalog
style only when the user explicitly delegates style selection or all settings.

On 2026-09-05, this distribution updated the vendored material to
a52e4456b8a4ccd4312069d6bc3755e2894dbc93 and re-merged the local adaptation
onto that base. Upstream's multi-size cover suite is preserved; the local retry
bound and the local generated-text status were reconciled with it and now apply
per target image rather than per run.

On 2026-09-29, this distribution updated the vendored material to
3fe93635e8842ca4f77ae472b8bb1c5a35b4a7d8 and re-merged the same local
adaptation onto that base. Upstream localization, platform-catalog.md, ratio
resolution, and the new cover styles (black-white-etching-editorial-cover,
minimal-light-tech, retro-futurism) are preserved.

These changes address the risk that an image model may misspell, omit, invent,
or crop visible text even when the intended wording is correct in the prompt.
Style or platform delegation never approves model-derived visible copy. These
changes do not claim that prompt-only or one-stage image generation can
guarantee exact text.

